<title>UK: Toyota unit sets C$125 million December 2002 bond.</title>
<headline>Toyota unit sets C$125 million December 2002 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers CIBC WoodGundy and Paribas.</p>
<p> BORROWER   TOYOTA CREDIT CANADA INC</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  TOYOTA MOTOR FINANCE NETHERLANDS BV (AAA/AAA)</p>
<p> AMT    C$125 MLN     COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    31.DEC.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.80    PAY DATE  S-11.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.20     SPREAD	+30 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/UK/CA</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.275     SELL CONC  1.60	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.0 PCT CANADA DUE SEPT 2002</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
